  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(x\\ne0\\) or \\(4\\) and \\(y\\ne0\\) or \\(6,\\) then \\(\\frac2x+\\frac3y=\\frac12\\) is equivalent to",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(4x+3y=xy\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(y=\\frac{4x}{6-y}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y}{3}=2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{4y}{y-6}=x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Multiplying by \\(2xy\\) gives \\(4y+6x=xy,\\) so \\(4y=x(y-6).\\) Since \\(y\\ne6,\\) \\[ x=\\frac{4y}{y-6}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Clear all three denominators at once",
        "After multiplying by \\(2xy,\\) isolate the terms containing \\(x\\) and factor"
      ],
